 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
 - CLI parsing accommodates further evaluation subcommands (e.g., `frai eval bias`).
 
+## Thresholds and CI Integration
+- `frai eval` supports `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option (repeatable) to gate CI pipelines on evaluation metrics.
+- A threshold passes when metric score ≥ minimum. Metrics with no score fail their threshold.
+- Exit code: 0 if all thresholds pass (or none set), 1 if any threshold fails.
+- Malformed thresholds (format or range) or unknown metrics exit with code 2 and list valid options.
+- JSON reports gain `passed` field and `thresholds` list; Markdown reports add a "Thresholds" section.
+- Works with custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations` since validation happens after evaluation.
+
 ## Follow-up Tasks
 1. Integrate real toxicity/bias models once provider abstraction is implemented (Phase 0 → Providers milestone).
 2. Extend datasets loader to support configurable schema mapping.
